    *place('The Black Lake',
           'Dark water stretching to the far shore, where the castle rises lit against the sky. A wooden jetty juts out from the rocks beside a boathouse. Reeds. Mist. And out on the water, slowly, something enormous breaks the surface and sinks again.',
           'Nobody. Day 4 Free time: the second diary page on the jetty. Door pin: steps up to the Courtyard.',
           [('The tentacle', 'The giant squid. Friendly, in its way. Throw it bread and it waves. Throw a spell at it and it throws the student into the lake (CON 10 or Stunned, and soaked).'),
            ('The jetty', 'Day 4: a diary page under a stone, the ink half-washed (quest).'),
            ('Skimming stones', 'A natural 20 on DEX: the stone skips all the way to the far side, and a light comes on in the castle window directly opposite.'),
            ('The boathouse', 'The boats from the first night. One is still damp, though nobody has used them since.'),
            ('Glacius on the water', 'A sheet of ice, ten feet across. Walk on it and it starts to crack.')]),

    *place('The old gamekeeper’s hut',
           'A stone hut with a giant-sized wooden door and a chimney trailing smoke. Pumpkins the size of armchairs fill a patch beside a wheelbarrow and a broken cart. Beyond the fence, the trees of the Forbidden Forest begin.',
           'Scamander most days. Day 3 Free time: the third rune tablet. Door pins lead to the Courtyard and into the Forest.',
           [('The giant door', 'Knock: a deep echo. Nobody answers. It is unlocked. Inside: one enormous chair, an enormous kettle, and a dragon egg (painted, a decoy) in the fireplace.'),
            ('The pumpkins', 'Huge. One has a face carved in it that winks.'),
            ('The crossbow', 'Old, heavy, unloaded. Scamander takes it off them politely.'),
            ('The cart and crates', 'Feed for creatures. The Thornbury knows exactly what each one is for. Taking some for Bramble: Creature treats.'),
            ('The fence at the Forest edge', 'Beyond it, the trees. A torn strip of grey hippogriff feather on a nail (Day 3 onwards).')]),

    *place('The Forbidden Forest',
           'Huge black trees, roots like arms, mist lying on the ground. Lanterns hang from branches here and there, left by someone, still burning. Pale blue mushrooms glow at the foot of a stump. In the dark between the trees, eyes, many of them, catching the light.',
           'Out of bounds. The centaur from Day 1 afternoon. Scamander on Day 3 Free time. Day 3: a Thornback Boar. Spin the Forest wheel on every visit.',
           [('The eyes in the dark', 'Owls, mostly. Some of them blink sideways. Ask the Thornbury what they are: “Better not to know.”'),
            ('The lanterns', 'Who hung them? Nobody knows. They lead deeper in, towards Bramble.'),
            ('The glowing mushrooms', 'Same as the greenhouse ones: eat one, glow for a block.'),
            ('The path', 'It goes deeper. Every time they go deeper, spin the wheel again.'),
            ('Bramble', 'From Day 3: deep in, afraid, a torn tag on her leg. See Where is Bramble? in the Quest Guide.')]),

